      "content": "Emphasized text: <em> Tag"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The <em> tag is used to emphasize text, making it stand out from the surrounding content. By default, browsers render emphasized text in italics. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<p>She whispered, \"Please, you must <em>believe</em> me.\"</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Browser Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "A webpage showing a paragraph including italic text.",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Like <strong>, the <em> element is also an inline element that doesn't extend the whole block."
    },
